1
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:20,440
THE CHARACTERS, BEHAVIORS, LOCATIONS,
ORGANIZATIONS, PROFESSIONS,

2
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:22,040
AND VARIOUS INCIDENTS
IN THIS SERIES ARE ENTIRELY FICTIONAL,

3
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,640
CREATED FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES ONLY,
WITHOUT ANY INTENTION TO REFERENCE

4
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:25,240
OR ENCOURAGE ANY ACTIONS
THAT MAY OCCUR IN REALITY.

5
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:26,840
PLEASE USE DISCRETION WHEN VIEWING

6
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:44,920
You guys just keep watching.

7
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,360
Hilarious.

8
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:52,600
Do you like taking photos?

9
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,760
It's a bit unusual,
you rarely come outside.

10
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,760
Why did you come out with Pan today?

11
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:04,120
Well…

12
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:06,880
I want to take photos of unusual things.

13
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:09,600
Unusual?

14
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,800
A waterfall is just a waterfall.

15
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:14,880
Taking pictures of people
is much stranger.

16
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,000
Feed me, feed me.

17
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:23,920
You can't eat.

18
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:28,360
Forehead kiss. Forehead kiss.

19
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,440
Woo!

20
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:32,760
You prick, you're gonna get it.

21
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:34,640
Damn!

22
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:07,560
Hey!

23
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:10,960
Hey!

24
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,400
How did you get inside?

25
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:14,880
This is my room.

26
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,280
Hey! Get out now!

27
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:17,560
I missed you.

28
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:22,000
You're like someone with mental problem.

29
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:23,480
Are you aware of that?

30
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:25,240
Isn't secretly taking photos
of random people

31
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:26,360
everywhere more crazy?

32
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:37,240
But they came out well.

33
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:39,760
A little bit of mental illness is fine.

34
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:41,880
I can forgive you.

35
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:42,960
Hey.

36
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:44,400
How did you come inside?

37
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:45,960
Did my mom see?

38
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:47,240
I just wanted to come in.

39
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,560
There was no one, so I came inside.

40
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:54,360
You're the one
who found Chee's body, right?

41
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:59,200
What are you saying? I don't get it.

42
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:04,160
When you came up,

43
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:08,880
I was the one
who called the police.

44
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:30,840
Hey,

45
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:34,080
you talk as if you don't feel anything.

46
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,680
Was I supposed to feel anything?

47
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:38,360
Do you have reason for coming here?

48
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:47,240
I just wanted to know,

49
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:51,640
the photo of Chee's body that you took,

50
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,080
where is it?

51
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,400
I didn't take it.

52
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:05,840
You take photos of everything that's dead.

53
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:08,920
Someone died right in front of you.

54
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:10,680
You wouldn't miss that chance.

55
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,760
I didn't bring my camera that day.

56
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:20,840
So…

57
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,720
You don't want to take
a photo of a dead person?

58
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,240
Hey!
Hey!

59
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:36,160
So,

60
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:37,240
can you leave now?

61
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:39,520
If my mom sees you, it'll be a problem.

62
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:44,160
Then…

63
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:46,920
Let's go take some photos.

64
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:33,920
Hey.

65
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:36,840
Where is the police station?

66
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:40,000
Drive that way. You'll see a market first.

67
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:41,800
Drive another two kilometers,
and you'll be there.

68
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:43,160
Wait.

69
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:46,920
With your tire looking like that,

70
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:49,080
you can only drive a short distance

71
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:50,160
before you won't get anywhere.

72
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:53,040
Why?

73
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,160
Oh.

74
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:03,400
How much do you charge to change it?

75
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:08,240
I'll do it for free.

76
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:09,840
Gook!

77
00:09:10,560 --> 00:09:11,800
-Gook!
-Yeah?

78
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:16,120
Take a look at her front tire for me.

79
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:17,800
Sure, Nai.

80
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,720
Why don't you wait inside my shop first?

81
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:25,680
I have a vending machine.

82
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:27,280
If you want to try your luck,

83
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:28,600
this one likes to eat coins.

84
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:50,320
MISSING PERSON

85
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:55,920
Gook, are you almost done?

86
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:57,720
Almost, Nai.

87
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:06,400
Does it smell?
Sorry.

88
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:10,760
Lucky today,

89
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:12,240
the machine didn't eat my coin.

90
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,640
MISSING PERSON

91
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:20,840
This case, has it been going on long?

92
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:24,520
Three years already.

93
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:27,360
It's hard to believe

94
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:28,720
a small district like this

95
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:31,360
would have a case like this.

96
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,920
For a small district like Waripasop,

97
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:35,640
this is a big deal.

98
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:38,280
I knew the missing woman.

99
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:40,360
But only briefly,

100
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,320
the locals here have already
forgotten all about it.

101
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
Waripasop…

102
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:49,200
Strange name.

103
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,400
There's a story behind it.

104
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:53,680
Want to hear it?

105
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:56,360
How so?

106
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:57,760
A long time ago,

107
00:10:58,440 --> 00:10:59,760
there was a well over there.

108
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:03,160
Before they settled down
and built the village,

109
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:05,480
they dug and found hundreds of skeletons.

110
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:07,640
So they named it Srapasop (Cemetery Pond).

111
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:13,000
They only changed it to Waripasop
a few decades ago.

112
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:15,160
Are you joking?

113
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:22,720
INSPECTOR TANG

114
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:25,520
-Hello.
-Okay.

115
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:26,960
All done?

116
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:28,360
All done, Nai.

117
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:57,600
I've been here
with my sister and her friends.

118
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:00,800
Chee's gang?

119
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:03,760
Mm.
You know them too?

120
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:07,760
Not long before my sister vanished,

121
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:09,960
this was the last place we came together.

122
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:14,640
Most people who go missing, if it's a man,

123
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:15,800
he ran away from home,

124
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:17,520
if it's a woman, it's what you'd expect.

125
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:25,200
Sometimes I wonder,

126
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:29,360
why isn't it me who vanishes instead?

127
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:41,840
If you vanished,

128
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:44,360
how would we meet?

129
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:02,400
Do you think Chees death

130
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:04,400
and your sister's disappearance

131
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:06,800
are related?

132
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,160
I don't know.

133
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:17,080
Then let's go back.
It's starting to get dark.

134
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:00,240
You want it or not?

135
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:10,480
If you're done, then it's finished. Go on.

136
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,320
-Hello.
-Hello.

137
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:27,440
Lieutenant Som, correct?

138
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:30,120
-Yes.
-I'm Sergeant Weerachon.

139
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:33,560
Inspector Tang has been waiting
for so long.

140
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:35,800
I was supposed to report in tomorrow,
wasn't I?

141
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:40,560
Yes, that's right.
It's just that, Chee, ah,

142
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:42,800
the son of Mr. Chawin,

143
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:45,520
one of the most influential figures
in our district was found murdered.

144
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:46,960
So things are a bit hectic today.

145
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:48,720
Either way,

146
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:50,680
please follow me,
I'll take you to the Inspector.

147
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:55,000
Inspector, permission to enter.

148
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:58,960
Excuse me.

149
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:02,720
Yes,
understood.

150
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:04,840
You don't need
to send a team from Bangkok.

151
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:06,520
I have it under control.

152
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:08,760
Goodbye.

153
00:15:26,640 --> 00:15:29,640
Sub-Lieutenant Niraphat Mankong,
reporting for duty.

154
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:46,000
A shiny new cop fresh from Bangkok.
Blah blah blah.

155
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:48,920
Let's skip the performance, shall we.

156
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,400
Honest question, why did you choose
to come here?

157
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:59,240
I like being close to nature.
And the forests here are beautiful.

158
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:00,360
Beautiful.

159
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,000
Here?

160
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:04,400
Fine.

161
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,000
There isn't much here.

162
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:07,800
There are only

163
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:10,120
people worth knowing,

164
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:12,200
and people you shouldn't
get involved with.

165
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:16,560
The income in this community

166
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:19,720
comes mainly from grain.

167
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:22,400
All the land belongs to Mr. Chawin.

168
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:28,440
And the law, that's my department.

169
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,280
Understood.

170
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:32,880
Take this file.

171
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:36,600
Mr. Chawin's son was found dead
this morning.

172
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:39,040
I'm putting you on the case.

173
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:42,640
Let's see

174
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:46,640
what a hotshot cop from Bangkok
can actually do.

175
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,200
Yes, sir.

176
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:56,280
Remember,

177
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:58,440
in a small town like this,

178
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:00,280
if you stand in the right place

179
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,480
and understand things correctly…

180
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:04,440
life will be very comfortable for you.

181
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:08,760
You may go.

182
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:02,960
I'm off.

183
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:05,160
Don't you want
to come inside and take photos?

184
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:08,960
Come on.

185
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:15,880
The murderer cut off the victim's fingers,

186
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:19,120
internal organs, and genitals.

187
00:20:20,720 --> 00:20:21,920
This case is not ordinary.

188
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:23,880
You need to close this case quickly.

189
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:27,840
If someone else dies,
we're all going to be in serious trouble.

190
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:31,040
Moving here and already this unlucky.

191
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:56,760
I'm sorry for your loss,

192
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:58,040
Chawin.

193
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:01,920
May I enter?

194
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:03,320
The curry is hot.

195
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:06,120
Of course.

196
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:24,040
-Que! Que!
-Coming.

197
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:26,800
Please get some water for Proud.

198
00:21:33,720 --> 00:21:35,040
A new worker?

199
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:37,360
My nephew.

200
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:38,440
Oh.

201
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:41,800
Please make yourself at home.

202
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:43,080
I'll excuse myself,

203
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:44,360
I still need to finish picking out
Cheei's clothes

204
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:47,200
Oh, would you like me to help you?

205
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:50,680
Choosing an outfit,
helping with the funeral…

206
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:53,040
I understand

207
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:55,280
what it's like to lose a child.

208
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:57,440
I know how hurt it is.

209
00:21:58,840 --> 00:22:01,040
Plus, Chee and Pan were dating.

210
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:04,440
Chee is also like my own child.

211
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:08,360
I'd rather do it myself.

212
00:22:11,040 --> 00:22:12,840
Que,
please take care of Auntie Proud.

213
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:27,800
Please have some water, auntie Proud

214
00:25:10,880 --> 00:25:11,920
How may I help?

215
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:14,360
I'm Sub-Lieutenant Niraphat.

216
00:25:14,920 --> 00:25:16,200
I've just transferred here.

217
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:17,560
You are Mr. Chawin, correct?

218
00:25:19,520 --> 00:25:20,520
A moment please.

219
00:25:21,280 --> 00:25:22,280
Ton.

220
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:25,360
Give Que a ride to the farm.

221
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:34,960
Please enter.

222
00:25:43,320 --> 00:25:44,320
I'm sorry.

223
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:45,760
I've been so busy lately

224
00:25:45,840 --> 00:25:48,280
that I didn't buy anything
to keep at home for guests

225
00:25:48,720 --> 00:25:49,720
It's alright.

226
00:25:50,160 --> 00:25:51,240
Water is enough.

227
00:25:54,640 --> 00:25:56,560
Tang didn't tell me…
Ah…

228
00:25:56,640 --> 00:25:57,640
Inspector Tang didn't tell me

229
00:25:57,720 --> 00:26:00,040
there'd be a new police officer here.

230
00:26:10,120 --> 00:26:11,120
Mr. Chawin,

231
00:26:11,760 --> 00:26:12,840
do you live alone?

232
00:26:28,240 --> 00:26:29,520
My wife passed away.

233
00:26:33,080 --> 00:26:34,080
I'm sorry.

234
00:26:34,760 --> 00:26:35,800
I wasn't aware.

235
00:26:41,160 --> 00:26:42,200
You've just arrived.

236
00:26:42,880 --> 00:26:44,240
It's not strange that you didn't know.

237
00:26:44,480 --> 00:26:45,920
I'm here today

238
00:26:46,800 --> 00:26:48,800
for Chee's murder case.

239
00:26:50,520 --> 00:26:53,040
Do you remember what Chee did that day

240
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:54,480
and who he met?

241
00:26:57,320 --> 00:26:58,400
I was at the farm.

242
00:26:58,960 --> 00:26:59,960
I've only met Ton,

243
00:27:00,040 --> 00:27:01,520
Ton, my driver,

244
00:27:01,880 --> 00:27:03,080
and he's mute.

245
00:27:03,160 --> 00:27:04,520
Chee went camping with his friends.

246
00:27:04,600 --> 00:27:06,240
Those regular ones.

247
00:27:06,320 --> 00:27:08,240
Nai, Joe, and M.

248
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:12,080
Around noon they came
to borrow fishing rods from my home.

249
00:27:23,760 --> 00:27:25,440
Let's go.

250
00:27:29,840 --> 00:27:31,200
Get out, what are you waiting for?

251
00:27:31,280 --> 00:27:32,520
That's how it should be,

252
00:27:32,600 --> 00:27:34,400
someone opening the door for us.

253
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:36,160
Where are you going?

254
00:27:41,360 --> 00:27:42,360
Hello, Dad.

255
00:27:50,760 --> 00:27:52,200
That's the last time I met him.

256
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:56,040
And

257
00:27:56,840 --> 00:27:59,040
did Chee said anything strange to you

258
00:27:59,600 --> 00:28:01,480
or anyone around him?

259
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:05,920
Chee has been strange
since his mom passed away.

260
00:28:06,800 --> 00:28:07,840
So I can't tell the difference

261
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:09,480
between when he's being strange

262
00:28:09,560 --> 00:28:10,600
and when he's being normal.

263
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:17,280
I'm suspecting Chee's death

264
00:28:18,360 --> 00:28:20,440
had a personal motive,

265
00:28:20,960 --> 00:28:22,920
like the killer wanted to humiliate him.

266
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:25,240
You're saying he has an enemy?

267
00:28:25,800 --> 00:28:26,840
Possibly.

268
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:29,840
That would be hard, officer.

269
00:28:30,160 --> 00:28:31,520
In this district,

270
00:28:32,080 --> 00:28:33,320
everyone is his enemy.

271
00:28:34,840 --> 00:28:36,800
He drives loudly, disturbing the locals.

272
00:28:37,800 --> 00:28:39,240
Gets drunk and picks fights with everyone.

273
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:42,120
Everyone in this district

274
00:28:42,560 --> 00:28:43,560
wants him dead.

275
00:29:11,920 --> 00:29:13,800
They usually don't sleep this early.

276
00:29:14,840 --> 00:29:16,120
Maybe because it's raining.

277
00:29:17,880 --> 00:29:19,360
We must catch the culprit,

278
00:29:19,880 --> 00:29:21,120
otherwise there will be more victims

279
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:25,160
I say we go back to rest, Sub-Lieutenant.

280
